  "description": "1) Southern live oak (T1)\rLocation: Back garden, right-hand side boundary (corner of Chelsham Road and Gauden Road).\rProposed works:\r\t?\tReduce overall crown height by up to 1.25 m, cutting back to previous pruning points.\r\t?\tSelective crown thinning of approximately 5 percent to improve light penetration to the understorey.\r\t?\tRemoval of minor internal and crossing branches to improve light levels and airflow.\rAll works to be carried out in accordance with BS3998:2010 Tree Work Recommendations.\r\r2) Bay tree (T2)\rLocation: Back garden, left-hand side.\rProposed works:\r\t?\tReduce crown height by approximately 0.5 to 1 m.\r\t?\tCrown thinning of approximately 5 percent.\r\t?\tLight formative pruning to create and maintain a spherical canopy shape.\rAll works to be carried out in accordance with BS3998:2010 Tree Work Recommendations.\r\rReasons for the works\r\t?\tTo reduce shading and increase daylight to the garden and understorey vegetation.\r\t?\tTo maintain the trees in good arboricultural condition through light crown management and selective thinning.\r\t?\tWorks are minor, non-invasive and do not affect the structural integrity or long-term health of the trees.\r\rFelling / replacement planting\rNo trees are proposed for felling. Replacement planting is therefore not required."
